# ── secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ── the raw store ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Immutable, content-hash addressed, and large. Full text is retained
# privately for verification and reprocessing — it is never republished
# and it does not belong in git.
raw_store/
data/raw/
*.warc
*.warc.gz

# A measurement's local corpus, same rule. `scripts/substitution_slice.py`
# writes 1,297 Reddit posts here so the sieve can be re-run for free; that is
# retained full text, so it stays out of git as firmly as the store proper.
# `git add -A` swept it in once — this is why the pattern is here and not in the
# script's docstring.
_substitution_slice/
_harvest_store/

# The unfiltered sweep's measurement population. Same rule, and one more
# reason: it carries a `delete_after` date in its manifest, and a corpus with
# a deletion date must not be the one thing in the repo that cannot be deleted.
_unfiltered_sweep/
_unfiltered_sweep_v2/
_control_sweep/

# The blog symbol census. Same two reasons, plus a third: it holds contexts
# quoted out of real articles, which is retained third-party text and is the
# one thing `docs/measurements/` must not accumulate.
_blog_so_sweep/

# The judge/ handoff export. The Reddit half comes from a committed fixture and
# would be harmless; the blog half is extracted article text drawn from the
# census corpus above, which carries a delete_after date. A retention date that
# only some copies of the text obey is not a retention date, so this goes to
# Engineer 2 out of band rather than through git.
_handoff/
# The same export, zipped for that out-of-band handover. A retention date the
# directory obeys and its zip does not is not a retention date either.
handoff.zip

# ── python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
# .python-version is deliberately NOT ignored (sign-off item 2). It pins the
# interpreter where pyenv and uv read it, so the pin enforces itself instead
# of being documented. Ignoring it would make the item a silent no-op.

# ── tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/

# ── local ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.db
*.sqlite3
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json

# ── generated output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
site/
exports/
_flattened_probe/

# E1's thread_context handoff. NOT a convenience entry.
#
# The blog half carries a `delete_after` date, and a retention date only some
# copies obey is not a retention date. Committing it would put a dated deletion
# obligation into git history, where deleting it later does not delete it.
#
# `git check-ignore _handoff/` already exited 0 before this line existed - a
# trailing-slash match on some other rule - while the files inside exited 1 and
# `git status` listed the directory as untracked. The directory reading as
# ignored while its contents were not is exactly the check that looks like a
# guarantee and is not.
_handoff/

# The spend ledger: a record of money actually spent (judge/spend_ledger.py).
# Operational data, not source, and it differs per machine — committing it would
# put one developer's spend on everyone else's admin page.
var/
_sweep_store/
